### Roles (modalidad JWT). Hasta que exista el login, pega un access token válido.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@token = <access_token>

### getAll: ADMIN, LOGISTICA, BASCULA, PLANTA, FINANZAS
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### getOne
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### create: nace SIN permisos; el nombre se guarda en mayúsculas -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "auditoria",
  "description": "Solo lectura"
}

### create: nombre repetido -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BASCULA"
}

### PUT -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/roles/6
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "AUDITORIA",
  "description": "Auditoría de liquidaciones"
}

### PATCH -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/roles/6
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Auditoría operativa"
}

### deactivate: sus usuarios pierden de inmediato esos permisos
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/roles/6/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### delete (físico); 409 si tiene asignaciones o concesiones
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/roles/6
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
